              "# Consumer sentiment drops to lowest level since 2016 US election\n- \"The loss was due to a host of issues including the partial government shutdown, the impact of tariffs, instabilities in financial markets, the global slowdown, and the lack of clarity about monetary policies,\" said Richard Curtin, chief economist for the Surveys of Consumers.\n- \"Aside from the direct economic impact from these various issues on the economy, the indirect effect meant that half of all consumers believed that these events would have a negative impact on Trump's ability to focus on economic growth,\" Curtin says",
